-- title:
--   Square-root logarithmic control of the local Taylor argument
-- statement:
--   For \(d\ge0\) and \(S,b\ge0\), put
--   \(T_n=S+\sqrt d\,\sqrt{2(b+4)\log n}\) and \(A_n=T_nS+S^2/2\). Define \(D=\frac32S^2+\sqrt d\,\sqrt{2(b+4)}\,S\).
--   Then all sufficiently large integers \(n\) satisfy
--   \[
--   A_n\le D\sqrt{\log n}.
--   \]
